AB  - The journey of drug discovery, from conceptualization to regulatory approval, is notoriously lengthy, costly, and prone to failure. Researchers have long sought to streamline this process, aiming for faster and error-free drug discovery. Traditionally, drug discovery involves numerous steps, from identifying biological targets associated with diseases to conducting clinical trials to marketing approval. The introduction of artificial intelligence (AI) in drug discovery represents a transformative advancement in the pharmaceutical industry, significantly altering the clinical development landscape. AI-designed drugs utilize sophisticated computational techniques, such as machine learning and deep learning, to predict molecular behavior, optimize lead compounds, and expedite the drug discovery process. This chapter delves into the profound impact of AI across various pharmaceutical sectors, including drug discovery and development, drug repurposing, and the enhancement of pharmaceutical productivity and clinical trials. The successful implementation of AI would not only reduce human workload but also achieve targets more efficiently. The chapter further explores how AI is revolutionizing each stage of the drug discovery process, the tools and techniques employed, ongoing challenges, and strategies to overcome these obstacles. Also, the future prospects of AI in the pharmaceutical industry, highlighting its potential to continually transform therapeutic development, are addressed.
