KW  - Frozen pretrained models
KW  - LiDAR camera fusion
KW  - Counterfactual controls
KW  - Feature-space repair
KW  - Fault detection
AB  - Extrinsic-calibration errors between LiDAR and cameras degrade fusion-based 3-D detectors that are deployed with fixed weights. This paper presents CaliPatch, which reads a planar calibration-parameter error directly from the pre-fusion bird’s-eye-view (BEV) features of a frozen BEVFusion detector and repairs the camera branch in place, without changing any host weight. The nuScenes-DD protocol crosses these parameter faults with independent modality dropout. On scenes excluded from observer fitting, direct repair under a shared 0.5 m/5° fault increases mAP by 3.05 ± 0.32 percentage points and recovers 70.5±7.5% of the same-warp oracle gain across three training seeds. Branch controls show modest effects from LiDAR substitution and similar median output amplitudes under common and camera-only feature warps. These responses point to camera-branch cues but do not isolate injector signatures. A dedicated BEVCalib estimator achieves greater recovery through the same warp, whereas CaliPatch has lower added latency in the measured implementation. Alarm gating reduces clean-input harm, but residual losses and single-camera failures limit the global repair. The evidence concerns shared supplied-parameter faults in one fixed rig and host, whose pretraining included the evaluation scenes.
ER  - 

