UR  - https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2666827026001465
KW  - Peer-to-peer learning
KW  - Adversarial robustness
KW  - Blockchain orchestration
KW  - Model provenance
KW  - Intrusion detection
KW  - EV charging security
KW  - Decentralized machine learning
AB  - Electric vehicle (EV) charging infrastructures require collaborative intrusion detection across distributed stakeholders without centralizing sensitive operational data. Existing federated and blockchain-assisted approaches often depend on a central aggregator, provide limited resilience to malicious participants, or use blockchain primarily as a passive logging layer. This paper presents BAROP, a Blockchain-Auditable and Adversary-Resilient On-Chain Peer-to-Peer learning framework for EV charging intrusion detection. BAROP replaces centralized aggregation with validation-gated checkpoint propagation, whereby each peer evaluates candidate models on private validation data, selectively adopts beneficial checkpoints, and performs warm-start local refinement. Model artifacts are stored off-chain, while blockchain records preserve checkpoint integrity, provenance, lineage, and participation states. A contribution-sensitive incentive mechanism further discourages low-quality and malicious behavior. BAROP is evaluated on the CICEVSE2024 Network Traffic benchmark under diverse adversarial scenarios involving up to 50% malicious peers. The evaluation includes comparisons with multiple decentralized baselines and a centralized Extreme Gradient Boosting (XGBoost) reference. Across the adversarial evaluation protocol, BAROP achieves an accuracy of 0.992, a macro-F1 score of 0.890, and a weighted-F1 score of 0.989, outperforming all decentralized baselines while remaining competitive with the centralized XGBoost reference. Additional experiments on the CICEVSE2024 Power Consumption and HPC/Kernel Events datasets, together with CICIoT2023, show that the same validation-gated mechanism remains effective across heterogeneous data modalities and beyond EV charging environments.
