AB  - This chapter discusses ethical issues arising from artificial intelligence and data mining technologies, and the responsible AI practices that may help to address these issues. We overview the issue of privacy in the context of data mining and technologies that can help address it, such as k-anonymity, differential privacy, and federated learning. We then tackle fairness and bias issues in machine learning, including the sources of bias and both technical and nontechnical interventions to mitigate them. Finally, we explain how AI alignment problems can potentially lead to harmful, or even catastrophic, results.
