KW  - Model watermarking
KW  - Efficient watermarking
KW  - Dynamic loss weight scheduler
KW  - Low-rank adaptation
KW  - Latent diffusion model
AB  - The rapid proliferation of Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) is driving a surge in model watermarking technologies, as the trained models themselves constitute valuable intellectual property. Current watermarking approaches primarily focus on modifying model parameters or altering sampling behaviors. However, as model sizes continue to grow, improving the efficiency of watermark embedding becomes essential to manage increasing computational demands. Prioritizing efficiency not only optimizes resource utilization, making the watermarking process more applicable for large models, but also mitigates potential degradation of model performance. In this paper, we propose an efficient watermarking method for Latent Diffusion Models (LDMs) based on Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA). The core idea is to introduce trainable low-rank parameters into the frozen LDM to embed a watermark, thereby preserving the integrity of the original model weights. Furthermore, a Dynamic Loss Weight Scheduler (DLWS) is designed to adaptively balance the objectives of watermark unobtrusiveness and watermark embedding, enabling the model to achieve effective watermark embedding with minimal impact on the quality of the output images. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed method enables fast and accurate watermark embedding and extraction with high-quality image generation, and remains effective under different payload settings. It also maintains robustness that is aligned with, and in some cases superior to, state-of-the-art methods. Moreover, the method remains effective across different datasets and several LDM backbones with compatible VAE decoding modules.
