KW  - Internet of vehicles
KW  - Unmanned aerial vehicle
KW  - Generative artificial intelligence
KW  - Blockchain
KW  - Task assignment
KW  - Intelligent transportation systems
AB  - The Internet of Vehicles (IoV) stands as a key component of Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS) with the emergence of Beyond 5G (B5G) and 6G networks, making it crucial for supporting autonomous driving, cooperative perception, and real-time vehicular services. However, achieving low latency, energy efficiency, and reliable task coordination remains challenging, primarily due to vehicle mobility, task dependencies, and the resource constraints of Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs). Current reinforcement learning methods remain reactive, lack scalability, and are susceptible to adversarial attacks. To address these limitations, this paper proposes a novel Generative AI and Blockchain Integrated Autonomy of IoV (GAIA-Chain), an integrated framework of autonomous task assignment in UAV-assisted IoV. GAIA-Chain combines a Generative Task Orchestrator (GTO) that automatically generates DAGs, Hierarchical Graph Mean-Field Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning (HGMF-MARL) for scalable UAV scheduling, a Generative Resource Allocator (GRA) for real-time resource allocation, Blockchain-anchored Federated Learning (FL-on-Chain) for secure model aggregation, predictive generative caching, and a safety and autonomy layer with constraint verification and risk-aware optimization. Extensive simulation results show that GAIA-Chain substantially reduces execution delays and energy consumption while satisfying Service-Level Agreements (SLA) requirements and ensuring both system transparency and the blockchain’s Byzantine resilience. Ultimately, by synergizing GAI, hierarchical multi-agent learning, and blockchain-based trust mechanisms, GAIA-Chain establishes a scalable, secure, and proactive paradigm to enable next-generation, UAV-assisted IoV.
ER  - 

